It's worth noting that Nethack predates the term "Open Source", or "Free
Software", or whatever.

Nethack was released in -87 -- that's the same year that gcc first came out,
and only three years after Stallman had announced the Gnu project. The
coolest thing around was SunOS, and VMS was still important.

The DevTeam of the time obviously liked the idea of sharing software and
hacking for fun, but I don't think you can expect them to share any number
of beliefs that have become common during the last fifteen years.

I find it useful to remind myself, once in a while, that NetHack comes from
the pre-GNU hacker culture.

